title: BobstartDay1
---
<<jump testNode>>
This is an example/Reference of how to set up dialog
The first node of Dialog MUST be named in this manner
The Starting Node set in the NPCData scriptable object attached
to the npcInteract
AND 'startDay1' or 'startDay2/3/4' depending on what day this dialog is for

! its best to keep all dialog for a character across days on one big YS script,
and break it up into different days instead of multiple scripts

How to check if player has an item?

You can check if the player has obtained evidence that has either been
SCANNED or NOT SCANNED using this command. 

<<if HasItem("objectID")>>
if the player has that object then anything written here
will be run 

! the objectID is the OBJECT HOLDERS NAME 
^ the inspectable object that has the interactableObj script 
NOT ITS CHILD 
<<endif>>


! if you want to check if the player has an item that 
WAS SCANNED. then you run this command a little differently.
<<if HasItem("objectID_scan")>>

! this will be the same objectID but with _scan 
^^^ do not edit the gameobject's name to include _scan,
the scripts will automatically add it to inventory with that 

<<endif>>

<<jump testNode>>
===
title: testNode
---
This node tests if the player has inspected the object 
<<if HasItem("ObjHolder")>>

The player has the item ObjHolder

<<endif>>

<<if HasItem("ObjHolder_scan")>>

The player has the item ObjHolder AND has scanned it

<<endif>>

===
